{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1189723-balefire","id":1189723,"title":"Balefire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-26T16:56:58-08:00","id":1189723,"title":"Balefire","content":"So this is possibly a dumb question. I am using bale fire for the first time in a long time (I like to keep it rare to keep it terrifying), and I just noticed there are 2 different sets of rules for it in W20. There is the BSD gift from the W20 core that says you gain a mutation if you take any damage, and that it's a diff 8 to soak. Then there is a section in BotW next to the bale fire flame thrower it says that bale fire is unsoakable and gives 2 battle scars in place of 1. Is the second one an amended rule? Or is it different based on different sources of bale fire? Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-26T21:18:28-08:00","id":1189767,"title":"","content":"The balefire flamethrower is different, likely because it is a weapon rather than 'raw' balefire. If you don't like it, feel free to change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:03:14-08:00","id":1189883,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I\u2019d interpret the flamethrower rules as the more technologically \u201cweaponized\u201d result, while the BSD Gift is dealing in its more raw form.<br /> <br /> But it\u2019s probably just different writers having different ideas so if you prefer one use that for the general rule, or suggest such to your storyteller","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}